    "q-10741": {
      "dom_id": "step-q10741",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "If $y=\\frac{11}{{x}^{9}},$ find $\\frac{dy}{dx}.$",
      "worked_solution": "We first rewrite the function as\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{11}{{x}^{9}}=11{x}^{-9}.\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the constant multiple and power rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(11{x}^{-9}) \\\\  & =11\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{-9}) \\\\  & =11\\cdot (-9){x}^{-9-1} \\\\  & =-99{x}^{-10} \\\\  & =-\\frac{99}{{x}^{10}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-10741-a",
